<title>UK: Rhone-Poulenc split seen unlikely - FT.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc split seen unlikely - FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc, the French chemicals and drugs group, appears to have ruled out splitting its pharmaceuticals and chemicals activities into two companies anytime soon, the Financial Times newspaper reported.</p>
<p>The company's chairman and chief executive, Jean-Rene Fourtou, said in an interview that he expected the company's share price would increase without a split, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
